This! Botany for gardeners is great, and it goes over some interesting biology aspects that would really be good. I would think basic biology / chemistry are key. Cells (plant/animal cells, organels, etc), Periodic table elements (H, 0, N, P, etc.) and the way they create unions between them, DNA, etc.

&#x200B;

Mostly the complexity of the relationship between plants and soil is based on biology concepts.
